    <name>
      <text>Limits of functions with several variables - Example 2.2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Determine if the limit of the function below exists or not. Fill in the missing computational steps.</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@question_func@}\)</p>
<br>
<p>Recall, \(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)} \displaystyle\frac{ f(x,y)}{g(x,y)} = \displaystyle \frac{\lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)}  f(x,y)}{ \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)}  g(x,y)} \) where \( \lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)}  g(x,y) \neq 0\) </p>
<br>
<p>First, let’s check if the limit of the function in the denominator will give us a zero. </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} ({@func_denom@}) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<br>
<p>From here, we can proceed as follows;</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@question_func@} = \displaystyle \frac{\lim_{(x,y) \to  ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})}  ({@func_num@}))}{\lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})}  ({@func_denom@})}=\)  [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<br>
<p>Therefore, we can say that the limit of this function [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Determine if the limit of the function below exists or not. Fill in the missing computational steps.</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@question_func@}\)</p>
<br>
<p>Recall, \(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)} \displaystyle\frac{ f(x,y)}{g(x,y)} = \displaystyle \frac{\lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)}  f(x,y)}{ \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)}  g(x,y)} \) where \( \lim_{(x,y) \to (x,y)}  g(x,y) \neq 0\) </p>
<br>
<p>First, let’s check if the limit of the function in the denominator will give us a zero. </p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} ({@func_denom@})&= ({@cc@}*{@var_x@}*{@var_y@}^2+{@cc+bb@}*{@var_y@})\\
&={@ta1@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>

<br>
<p>From here, we can proceed as follows;</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})} {@question_func@} = \displaystyle \frac{\lim_{(x,y) \to  ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})}  ({@func_num@}))}{\lim_{(x,y) \to ({@var_x@},{@var_y@})}  ({@func_denom@})}={@ta2@}\) </p>
<br>
<p>Therefore, we can say that the limit of this function exists</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
